<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sanlam ends talks on SA Druggists link.</title>
<headline>Sanlam ends talks on SA Druggists link.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's mutual assurance giant Sanlam said on Tuesday it had terminated talks on a possible closer link between its healthcare businesses and South African Druggists Ltd.</p>
<p>Sanlam's industrial holding arm Sankorp, a key stakeholder in Malbak Ltd which is currently unbundling, had previously said it intended to reduce its stake in Malbak's unbundled units &quot;with the possible expection of SA Druggists&quot;.</p>
<p>Following the termination of discussions between the drugs firm and Sanlam Heath/Sanmed, Sankorp will now explore ways to reduce its shareholding in SA Druggists over the next few years.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
